    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d935">

                <pb facs="1241" n="1231" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg1231"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/5–2745</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Makins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Clayton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-27">May 27, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Clayton</hi>: I enclose a memorandum of
                    the preliminary views of His Majesty’s Government concerning the employment of
                    German labour as a form of reparation.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>This matter was raised informally with Mr. Eden in San Francisco by Mr.
                        Pauley and Mr. Eden undertook to ascertain the preliminary views of His
                        Majesty’s Government on his return to London.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Mr. Eden would like to know the opinion of the United States Government on
                        this subject, and I should be very glad of an opportunity to discuss the
                        question with you in the near future.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>I am sending a copy of this letter to Mr. McCloy<anchor n="24"
                            xml:id="d935-f1"/> as I understand that he took part in the discussions
                        at San Francisco.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roger Makins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d935-a1.xml" xpointer="d935-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d935-f1" n="24" xml:id="d935-f1-content">
                <p>Assistant Secretary of War John J. McCloy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
